# PLACEHOLDER — the Grow Lamp, an LED panel hung on copper chains.
#
# The model is a 14x3x14 copper panel (y 4..7) on two vanilla copper chains. Only three things are
# drawn here, and each face uses a region of its texture:
#   grow_lamp_top      the panel's top, uv 1..15 — vents over the driver
#   grow_lamp_side     the panel's edge, uv rows 0..2 — a copper band over the lamp's own edge row,
#                      so a powered lamp reads lit from the side too
#   grow_lamp_bottom   the lamp face, uv 1..15
# The rest of each 16x16 is filler that nothing shows (the particles are the top's).
#
# The face is vanilla's redstone_lamp and redstone_lamp_on, pixel for pixel, turned violet: the
# recipe wraps a redstone lamp, and the lamp should show it. Each colour keeps its lightness and
# saturation and takes the hue of the old diodes (264°); the two that landed next to the old lit
# diode colours were snapped onto them (8A3CFF, CDB0FF). uv 1..15 shows the lamp's 14x14 inside and
# crops its frame — the copper band is the frame now.
#
# The lamp face is the only purple there is: Minecraft light has no colour, so the lamp lights the
# world white like every other light source. Violet since 2026-09-15, to read as UV and blurple LED
# grow lights; the redstone lamp's face since 2026-10-03, when it had been a grid of diodes.
#
# It was a full copper cube until 2026-09-15, whose only lit face was the underside: a powered lamp
# looked unpowered from every other angle, and in daylight that read as "gives no light".
#
#   python3 mctex.py render \
#     textures-src/grow_lamp.mctex -o src/main/resources/assets/hempdustry/textures --preview

@palette default
a = 6D3421      copper, deep shadow
b = 8A4129
c = A4553A      copper mid
