# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LabPBR specular maps (_s), for shader packs set to resource-pack PBR (Complementary: RP_MODE
# labPBR). Same drawings, so every pixel lines up with its art. Per the LabPBR standard:
#   R  perceptual smoothness        G  F0, or 230-255 = a hardcoded metal — 234 is copper
#   B  porosity / SSS (0 here)      A  emission 0-254; 255 means "none" and is what non-glowing
#                                      pixels carry
# The copper housing is metal 234; the lamp face is a dielectric (G 10, ~4%), its dark lines rough
# and its panes smooth. Lit, the panes glow 200, 230 and 254 by brightness — which is what makes a
# LabPBR pack render them as a violet UV light. Nothing here can colour the light the lamp casts; see crops.md, the Grow Lamp.

@palette spec
a = 46EA00FF
b = 5AEA00FF
c = 6EEA00FF
d = 82EA00FF
e = 96EA00FF
f = AAEA00FF
k = 3C0A00FF
l = 460A00FF
m = C80A00FF
n = C80A00FF
o = C80A00FF
p = DC0A00FF
q = DC0A00FF
r = DC0A00FF
s = 3C0A00FF
t = 460A00FF
u = C80A00FF
v = C80A00FF
w = D20A00FF
x = DC0A00FF

@palette spec_lit extends=spec
v = C80A00C8
w = D20A00E6
x = DC0A00FE

@texture block/grow_lamp_side_s from=band palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_side_on_s from=band_on palette=spec_lit type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_top_s from=block/grow_lamp_top palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom_s from=lamp palette=spec type=block
@texture block/grow_lamp_bottom_on_s from=lamp_on palette=spec_lit type=block
